# Prettier's MDX/remark parser corrupts fenced code blocks that are children of a
# custom JSX component (e.g. a Python code fence inside <CodeWalkthrough>...</CodeWalkthrough>):
# it strips indentation from later statements in the block. Content pages routinely nest
# code fences inside doc components, so hand-format these instead of trusting `prettier --write`.
# See ADR-0003 for the same class of MDX/JSX-nesting fragility in the Mermaid component.
apps/handbook/src/content/docs/**/*.mdx

# Episode transcripts are a verbatim record of what was spoken, and Prettier's
# markdown parser rewrites the words: `__del__` in a sentence about Python came
# back as `**del**`. They are generated by `renderTranscript`, never hand-edited,
# so there is nothing for a formatter to tidy and everything for it to corrupt.
apps/handbook/src/transcripts/*.md
